  "readme": [
    {
      "section": "@zhongjingwei/dsh-model-retry",
      "text": "[](https://github.com/502399493zjw-lgtm/dsh-model-retry/actions/workflows/ci.yml)\n\nEnglish | [中文](README.zh.md)\n\nDeepSeek Harness Web plugin for configuring active providers' model-request retry budget from **Settings → General**.\n\n> Compatibility: pinned to stock DSH `0.1.0-rc.8`. rc.8 moved retry ownership into provider profiles, so this version writes each active normal provider's `retryPolicy.maxRetries` through the published settings API."
    },
    {
      "section": "Demo",
      "text": "The demo uses stock DSH `0.1.0-rc.8` and a plugin tarball packed from this source, all under an isolated `DSH_HOME`. It changes the retry budget from `2` to `5`, then uses DSH's deterministic local LLM mock to return retryable server errors on attempts 1–5 and succeed on attempt 6. Session-title generation is disabled so those six mock requests belong only to the demonstrated model request. DSH executes and reports the retries; the plugin owns the shared retry-budget setting."
    },
    {
      "section": "Install",
      "text": "For stock rc.8:\n\n```bash\ndsh plugin --profile web add @zhongjingwei/dsh-model-retry@0.1.0-rc.9\n```\n\nRestart Web after installation. Remove the plugin with:\n\n```bash\ndsh plugin --profile web remove @zhongjingwei/dsh-model-retry\n```"
    },
    {
      "section": "Behavior",
      "text": "- Adds one numeric retry-count row to Settings → General and shows its provider scope.\n- Accepts finite, non-negative integers, including `0`.\n- Discovers active configurable providers through `llm.providers` and uses revision-fenced `settings.mutate` calls.\n- Writes `retryPolicy.maxRetries` for normal/default policies while preserving existing backoff and retryable-code fields.\n- Leaves `always` policies unlimited and leaves retry execution/backoff behavior owned by DSH."
    },
    {
      "section": "Development",
      "text": "```bash\npnpm install\npnpm test\npnpm run build\npnpm run verify:package\n\nThe package is an external Cordis plugin and does not patch DSH core."
    },
    {
      "section": "License",
      "text": "MIT"
    }
  ],
